            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full. The change adds an evidence check to 'roles append' that fails closed: a completed review-report is stored only if its evidence matches the stored review files, and a check that cannot run (no repository, git or store failure) refuses the record.",
              "Records that need no evidence (anything but a completed review-report) skip the check before the working directory is consulted, so baseline behavior is preserved for them, and the interrupted-report test covers this.",
              "The check runs after flag/record matching and before the store is created or written, so a refused record is never persisted. engine/cmd/roles.go lines 294-298 show the ordering.",
              "No secrets, injection, path traversal, or data-loss vector was found. Digests are compared against stored files, and the error text only echoes the evidence kind and ref. Tests use temporary directories and a temporary state home.",
              "Existing callers keep their behavior: runRolesTest now injects the production-style check over empty deps, which only affects review-report records, and those fail closed in that test setup."
            ]
          }
        }
