            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths in full from the supplied patches.",
              "engine/cmd/roles.go:294-298: the evidence check runs after the record has been read and matched to its flags and before the store is created, so a refused record is never written. The fail path returns after exit.",
              "engine/cmd/roles_evidence.go: a record that needs no evidence returns nil before the working directory is read. A check that cannot run (no working directory, no repository, git or store failure) is wrapped with a clear message, so the check fails closed. EvidenceError values pass through unchanged.",
              "engine/cmd/roles_evidence_test.go covers the check being asked before storing, with refusal, acceptance and flag mismatch. It covers records from review record and review verify being accepted. It covers missing evidence and digest mismatches for the diff, result and verifier kinds, plus a result file modified after recording. It covers an interrupted report that needs no repository, and the built binary run in the repository and outside any repository. Each case asserts exit code, stderr, stdout and whether the record was stored, so the externally observable behavior is proved.",
              "engine/cmd/roles_test.go: runRolesTest keeps the old call shape through a check built over empty deps. Records that need no evidence behave as before, and records that need evidence fail closed. This is deliberate and matches the test comments.",
              "No regressions found for input that was valid at the baseline except the intended new refusal of review-reports whose evidence does not match the stored files, which is the requested behavior."
            ]
          }
